Id: sctl006w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Turn off Internet Sharing, or set both forwarding keys to 0 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

The Mac forwards packets between its networks, as a router does: the
forwarding switch named (IPv4, IPv6, or each reported in turn) is on.
That is Internet Sharing left on (System Settings, General, Sharing),
which also opens the Mac to whatever the other side sends, or a switch
someone set by hand. A Mac that is not meant to route should not
forward:
  # sysctl -w net.inet.ip.forwarding=0 net.inet6.ip6.forwarding=0
and keep both keys at 0 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
